{"name":"New Life","hex":"#7c916e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"new","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Newar."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Recently made, or created.","Of recent origin; having taken place recently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/new"},{"term":"life","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of organisms preceding their death, characterized by biological processes such as metabolism and reproduction and distinguishing them from inanimate objects; the state of being alive and living.","The status possessed by any of a number of entities, including animals, plants, fungi, bacteria, and sometimes viruses, which have the properties of replication and metabolism."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To replace components whose operational lifetime has expired."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/life"}],"entries":[{"title":"Born again","blocks":[{"text":"To be born again, or to experience the new birth, is a phrase, particularly in evangelical Christianity, that refers to a \"spiritual rebirth\", or a regeneration of the human spirit. In contrast to one's physical birth, being \"born again\" is distinctly and separately caused by the operation of the Holy Spirit. It occurs when one accepts Jesus Christ as their personal Lord and Savior, upon which point they are said to have \"died\" to their sinful state and been born into a new, saved life. While all Christians are familiar with the concept from the Bible, it is a core doctrine of the denominations of the Moravian, Methodist, Plymouth Brethren, Pentecostal and Radical Pietist churches along with other evangelical Christian denominations, such as evangelical Quakers and Baptists. These churches stress Jesus's words in the Gospels: \"Do not be astonished that I said to you, 'You must be born from above.'\". Their doctrines also hold that to be \"born again\", and thus \"saved\", one must have a personal and intimate relationship with Jesus Christ."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Chancel_of_White_Memorial_Wesleyan_Methodist_Church.jpg/330px-Chancel_of_White_Memorial_Wesleyan_Methodist_Church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Born_again","wikidata":"Q613015"},{"title":"New Life (Monica album)","blocks":[{"text":"New Life is the seventh studio album by American singer Monica, released by RCA Records on April 6, 2012. It marked the singer's debut release with the label following the dissolution of her former label, J Records in October 2011. A musical continuation of her commercially successful previous album Still Standing (2010), Monica began working on the album only weeks after the release of the former. She returned to work with frequent collaborators; writers and producers including Bryan-Michael Cox, Jermaine Dupri, Missy Elliott, and Cainon Lamb, as well as such as singer and songwriter Rico Love, whose songs replaced much of her cousin, producer Polow da Don's original material."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/59/New-Life.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Life_(Monica_album)","wikidata":"Q7009814"},{"title":"Life","blocks":[{"text":"Life is the capacity in matter, formed of one or more units called cells, for processes such as cell signalling, homeostasis, metabolism, cell growth, adaptation, response to stimuli, and reproduction. All life eventually reaches a state of death. Many philosophical definitions of living systems have been proposed, such as self-organising systems. Defining life is further complicated by viruses, which replicate only in host cells, and the possibility of extraterrestrial life, which could be very different from life on Earth. Life exists all over the Earth in air, water, and soil, with many ecosystems forming the biosphere. Some of these are harsh environments occupied only by extremophiles. The life in a particular ecosystem is called its biota."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg/330px-Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life","wikidata":"Q3"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Nicodemus_Jesus.jpg/500px-Nicodemus_Jesus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Nicodemus_Jesus.jpg/1280px-Nicodemus_Jesus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Nicodemus_Jesus.jpg/500px-Nicodemus_Jesus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jesus and Nicodemus, painting by Alexandre Bida, 1874","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANicodemus_Jesus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Saint_Peter%27s_Basilica_facade%2C_Rome%2C_Italy.jpg/500px-Saint_Peter%27s_Basilica_facade%2C_Rome%2C_Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Saint_Peter%27s_Basilica_facade%2C_Rome%2C_Italy.jpg/1280px-Saint_Peter%27s_Basilica_facade%2C_Rome%2C_Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Saint_Peter%27s_Basilica_facade%2C_Rome%2C_Italy.jpg/500px-Saint_Peter%27s_Basilica_facade%2C_Rome%2C_Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Saint Peter's Basilica façade, Rome, Italy","link":"https://en.wikipe